P2PDMA stage-1 fail-the-write ARM gating -- compile the write-failure
completion arms out on pre-6.11 kernels. Companion to
0008-p2pdma-feature-flag-gating.patch (which gates the advertise machinery
that both featured variants share); split out of 0008 per the spec §6 amendment
(2026-07-03).

Stage-1 fail-the-write (feature branch p2pdma) adds error-path sites on top of
the advertise feature: raid1/raid10 tag P2P master bios at submit (set_bit
R1BIO_P2P / R10BIO_P2P keyed on md_bio_is_p2pdma()); a leg completing
BLK_STS_INVAL/BLK_STS_TARGET on a tagged bio marks R1BIO_P2PError /
R10BIO_P2PError and fails the whole write loud (master forced to BLK_STS_INVAL
in call_bio_endio / raid_end_bio_io) instead of silently diverging the mirrors;
reads keep their real status. Gate the six consumers on HAVE_BLK_FEAT_PCI_P2PDMA
(dkms/Makefile.in feature_flags probe): the two end_write_request completion
arms, both master-status overrides, and both end_read_request read-fidelity
blocks. The R1BIO_P2P*/R10BIO_P2P* enum bits and the submit-time detection sites
stay deliberately UNGATED: with md_bio_is_p2pdma() folded to constant false (by
0008), `if (md_bio_is_p2pdma(bio)) set_bit(...)` is provably dead code the
compiler discards, so gating them would add #ifdef noise for zero object-code
change. The write-arm gate rewrites `} else if (...)` to `} else` + `#endif` +
`if (...)` so the flag-off preprocess reduces to the pre-feature
`if/else if/else` chain with braces balanced in both personalities.

Why guarded on R10BIO_P2PError: the arm code exists ONLY in the full stage-1
fail-the-write tree. The kit builds two featured variants through this same
patch pipeline -- gdsM (meshstor-main, full stage-1 present) and gds1 (a pin
that advertises the feature but has fail-the-write ABSENT). 0008's advertise
gating applies to both, but these arm hunks reference R1BIO_P2PError /
R10BIO_P2PError and the P2P write arms, which the advertise-only pin does not
contain -- so applying them there would reject against code that does not exist.
The `0011-...patch.when` guard keys on raid10.c:R10BIO_P2PError, a token present
only in stage-1 trees, so this patch self-excludes from the advertise-only
variant.

Because 0011 is only ever applied to a stage-1 tree, its hunks use ordinary
context -- EXCEPT the raid10 read-fidelity hunk, which keeps minimal symmetric
context (leading anchor `} else if (!raid1_should_handle_error(bio)) {`,
trailing `uptodate = 1;`): in the composed meshstor-main tree the md-latency-ewma
branch inserts its fold-kick block directly above that anchor (before
`set_bit(R10BIO_Uptodate ...)`), so diff-default three-line context anchors on
shape-specific lines and rejects at --fuzz=0 on whichever p2pdma-bearing
composition it wasn't diffed against. regenerate.sh preserves this patch (.when
guard); edit by hand, keep that hunk minimal.

Source-level, not a header shim: it adds preprocessor structure to drivers/md.

